	  <br>
	  <br>


          Greetings all!<br>
          <br>
          Last night, well over 100 leaders and officers of the guilds of Fennin Ro met in the Temple of Solusek Ro in order to listen to ideas for embettering roleplay on a server-wide scale. Jythri duan'Cliar of The Soerbaird and Jubal Kinseeker of the Sterling Order of Knights proposed before the collected assembly a flexible system of regional law and government, which they have termed 'Common Law'.<br>
          <br>
          Discussion of these concepts among Fennin Ro residents begin today on the Fennin Ro Guild Hall (http://www.sok.org/fenninro). There's a lot of work to do ahead of us. But even if the idea of Common Law fails, we, the leaders of Fennin Ro, have already succeeded--we have begun to set a precedent for communication and interaction that will go a long way to improving our world.<br>
          <br>
          The Fennin Ro Guild Hall can be found here:<br>
          <a href="http://www.sok.org/fenninro/">http://www.sok.org/fenninro/</a><br>
          <br>
          The minutes of the Council of the Collective may be found here:<br>
          <a href="http://www.sok.org/fenninro/council1.htm">http://www.sok.org/fenninro/council1.htm</a><br>
          <br>
          The outline of the Common Law system may be found here:<br>
          <a href="http://www.sok.org/fenninro/commonlaw.htm">http://www.sok.org/fenninro/commonlaw.htm</a><br>
          <br>
          The forums where these ideas will be discussed may be found here:<br>
          <a href="http://www.sok.org/cgi-bin/fenninro/Ultimate.cgi">http://www.sok.org/cgi-bin/fenninro/Ultimate.cgi</a><br>
          <br>
          <br>
          We are excited about the support many have shown thus far, and are ready to work to make Norrath a more interesting and alive place for us all to be.<br>
          <br>
          SIDE NOTE: I apologize to any guild who thought the primary reason for the meeting was to discuss the Fennin Ro split. That topic has been discussed at length on the Fennin Ro Guild Hall for a couple of weeks now, and most of the guilds who have spoken there are resolved to stay. We did speak briefly of the split at the end of the meeting, many leaders there expressing disgust at the poor options offered by Verant on the matter, and many re-stated their resolve to remain on Fennin.<br>
          <br>
          Thank all of you again, for your support and attendance! We look forward to the futhre.<br>
          <br>
          Listen and Live.
